      "source": [
        "## Practice 3: Dependency Approval Workflows\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** Control which dependencies enter your ML stack by:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Defining rules for high‑impact categories (ML frameworks, crypto, network, subprocess)  \n",
        "- Requiring security/legal review for risky items  \n",
        "- Documenting SLAs and checks  \n",
        "\n",
        "This is encoded in `approval_policy.json` and supports consistent, auditable decisions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"PRACTICE 3: DEPENDENCY APPROVAL WORKFLOWS\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nWhy Approval Workflows?\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Prevent supply chain attacks\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Ensure license compliance\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Avoid unmaintained packages\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Control technical debt\")\n",
        "\n",
        "approval_policy = {\n",
        "    \"rules\": [\n",
        "        {\n",
        "            \"category\": \"ml-frameworks\",\n",
        "            \"packages\": [\"torch\", \"tensorflow\", \"jax\"],\n",
        "            \"requires\": \"security-review\",\n",
        "            \"reason\": \"Core ML frameworks have high impact\"\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        {\n",
        "            \"category\": \"restrictive-licenses\",\n",
        "            \"licenses\": [\"GPL-3.0\", \"AGPL-3.0\"],\n",
        "            \"requires\": \"legal-review\",\n",
        "            \"reason\": \"May conflict with commercial use\"\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        {\n",
        "            \"category\": \"new-publishers\",\n",
        "            \"criteria\": \"package_age < 90 days OR publisher_reputation < 3/5\",\n",
        "            \"requires\": \"security-review\",\n",
        "            \"reason\": \"Unknown packages need vetting\"\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        {\n",
        "            \"category\": \"high-risk-categories\",\n",
        "            \"package_types\": [\"crypto\", \"network\", \"subprocess\"],\n",
        "            \"requires\": \"security-review\",\n",
        "            \"reason\": \"High-risk functionality\"\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"approval_process\": {\n",
        "        \"security-review\": {\n",
        "            \"reviewers\": [\"security-team@company.com\"],\n",
        "            \"sla_days\": 5,\n",
        "            \"checks\": [\"CVE scan\", \"Source code review\", \"Maintainer reputation\"]\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        \"legal-review\": {\n",
        "            \"reviewers\": [\"legal-team@company.com\"],\n",
        "            \"sla_days\": 3,\n",
        "            \"checks\": [\"License compatibility\", \"IP concerns\"]\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "with open('approval_policy.json', 'w') as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(approval_policy, f, indent=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"✓ Created approval_policy.json\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n[Approval Policy Rules]\")\n",
        "for rule in approval_policy['rules']:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{rule['category'].upper()}:\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Requires: {rule['requires']}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Reason: {rule['reason']}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[Example: Adding PyTorch to Project]\")\n",
        "print(\"\\nStep 1: Developer submits dependency request\")\n",
        "print(\"  Package: torch==2.0.1\")\n",
        "print(\"  Justification: Required for transformer model training\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nStep 2: Automated check triggers approval workflow\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ Package matches 'ml-frameworks' rule\")\n",
        "print(\"  → Assigns to security-team@company.com\")\n",
        "print(\"  → SLA: 5 business days\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nStep 3: Security team reviews\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ CVE scan: No critical vulnerabilities\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ Source code: Official PyTorch repository\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ Maintainer: Meta/PyTorch team (trusted)\")\n",
        "print(\"  → APPROVED\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nStep 4: Package added to approved list\")\n",
        "print(\"  → Developer can now use torch in requirements\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n✅ Benefits:\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Prevent risky dependencies\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Clear ownership and accountability\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Documented approval decisions\")\n",
        "print(\"  • Automated enforcement\")"
      ]
    },
    {
